+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""C6 W8A8 CUDA cuEvent timing harness (measurement only, protocol-shaped).
+
+Measures the four frozen C6 CUDA W8A8 opcodes on the 12 W8J GEMM shapes:
+
+    qmatmul_s8s8_s32            m x k  @  k x n   (int8 -> int32 device kernel)
+    quantize_per_token_s8       m x k             (f32 -> int8 per-row)
+    dequantize_s8               m x n             (int8 codes x per-row scale -> f32)
+    dequantize_epilogue_bf16    m x n             (int32 acc x row x col scale -> bf16)
+
+Shape set = ``vendor_gemm_matrix.SHAPES`` x ``M_VALUES`` (the W8J 12-shape gate):
+    (k,n) in {(1024,32),(1024,5120),(1024,7168),(1024,8192),(2048,1024),(3584,1024)}
+    m      in {1, 5}
+so every opcode is measured on 12 shapes (48 cases total).  The per-opcode
+shape mapping keeps the W8J (m, k, n) row intact: qmatmul uses (m,k)x(k,n),
+quantize (m,k), dequantize and epilogue (m,n).
+
+Method (docs/PERF_MEASUREMENT_PROTOCOL.zh-CN.md + ERR-0004 + B3a):
+
+  * cuEvent timing only (never host wall as the headline);
+  * warmup W=5 per case, then R measured rounds per case (default 21);
+  * median / min / p95(nearest-rank) / max / sample stdev / cv /
+    p95_over_median, and the ERR-0004 outlier rule
+    ``|x - median| > max(3*1.4826*MAD, max(1us, 0.02*median))`` with
+    ``outlier_ratio > 0.10 -> UNSTABLE``;
+  * in-window cuEvent rate calibration (two host ``sleep`` gaps inside event
+    pairs, plus a long-batch corrected-vs-host-wall agreement check); raw and
+    corrected numbers are both reported;
+  * >= 2.0 s clock warmup payload with ``clocks.sm`` sampling under load;
+  * nvidia-smi fingerprint before/after and GPU-wide utilization samples
+    during the run (a foreign/user workload on the shared GamePC is recorded
+    rather than hidden).
+
+The measured kernel time is the cuEvent span around exactly the launch the
+runtime's ``_w8a8_launch`` performs (same ``module``/``function`` handle, same
+``(grid, block, shared)`` geometry, same parameter order).  The public
+``run_w8a8_*`` entry points are exercised separately for host-side dispatch
+overhead on one representative shape per opcode, because their pure-Python
+input marshalling is O(elements) and would dominate a per-round loop.
+
+Everything is UNGATED: WSL2 guest, no cpufreq control, shared non-quiet
+window.  No number produced here is a cross-platform speedup claim.
+
+Usage (GamePC WSL2):
+
+    PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY=1 PYTHONPATH=<tree>/python python3 \
+        scripts/perf/c6_timing_harness.py --output /tmp/c6-raw.json
+
+Local pre-flight (no GPU, compiles the 48 artifacts only):
+
+    PYPTO_X_PORTABLE_ONLY=1 PYTHONPATH=python python3 \
+        scripts/perf/c6_timing_harness.py --build-only --output /tmp/c6-build.json
+"""
+
